{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he took.</b> He mentioned above that the children of Israel who were alive in that generation went up; also the distinguished one among them went up with them, for through him they had come down to Egypt, and he adjured them before his death that they should say thus to their children and their children to their children. And behold, Moses occupied himself with fulfilling the oath, so that guilt would not come upon Israel. For we saw that the princes of Israel swore to the Gibeonites, and they swore to them only on the condition that they were far away, as they said; and after they were found to be close, it would have been proper not to keep their oath, and not to transgress — they and all Israel — the commandment 'you shall not leave alive any soul' (Deuteronomy 20:16). Only for the honor of HaShem did they act, so as not to profane it. And after many years HaShem punished the children of Israel because Saul allowed the Gibeonites who were in Nob, the city of the priests, to be killed:" "And he mentioned bones, for all the flesh and skin worms will consume and it will putrefy, and they will not remain after a few years — only the bones."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:14.852004677Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}